{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794242238,"nonce":"V1eWm6Aw0se/blzSNROKTTqBFnU=","title":"CSS padding/margin longhands replace the whole box","message":"`padding-right: 6px` on its own parses to a padding rect of `0 6px 0 0`\n(`blinc_css` parser/properties/apply.rs starts from zeros when the style has no\npadding yet), so a rule that only means to change one side zeroes the other\nthree sides set by an earlier rule. CSS cascades each longhand separately.\n\nSeen with cn tabs: `.cn-tabs-trigger--closable { padding-right: ... }` after\n`.cn-tabs-trigger--md { padding: ... }` wiped the trigger's top/left/bottom\npadding. Worked around in cn_styles by restating the full shorthand per size.\n\nFix: hold padding and margin per side (`Option\u003cf32\u003e` each) in ElementStyle so\nthe cascade merges sides, and apply only the sides a rule sets. Same check for\nmargin-*, border-*-width, inset longhands.","files":null}]}